    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `postcode` to owners: a 4-digit value that, when present, must fall in the range for the city's region (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099); unknown regions accept any 4-digit value; absent postcodes stay accepted (backward-compatible). Out-of-range and malformed postcodes are rejected with 400; valid ones are stored and returned.\n\n**How it's wired (keeping structural impact low):**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `postcode` property (with `^\\d{4}$` pattern \u2192 the malformed-length 400) to `OwnerFields`, and a class-level `x-class-extra-annotation` for the cross-field rule. No code touched to get the field/pattern.\n- **`ValidPostcode` + `ValidPostcodeValidator`** (2 new, tiny cohesive classes) \u2014 the region-range check lives here, in a class whose surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) is ~zero. The validator reuses the existing `Locality.of(city)` region table. Because it's a class-level Bean Validation constraint on the DTO, the existing `@Valid` on the controller body triggers it automatically \u2014 **no controller change** (avoiding the large `OwnerRestControllerV1`/`addOwner` costs).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 a plain field plus a straight getter/setter (CC 1 each), the minimum needed for JPA persistence.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 one `postcode` column for the test database.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps `postcode` both directions, so the mapper needed no edits. I scoped the DB change to hsqldb (the test DB) following the existing repo convention \u2014 h2 (the default profile) auto-updates its schema, and postgres/mysql schemas are already intentionally out of sync with the entity.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I did **not** add the `postcode` column to the postgres/mysql `schema.sql` files, matching the repo's existing pattern where those already omit columns like `customer_code`. If you deploy on postgres/mysql without `ddl-auto`, say the word and I'll add it there too.",
